# Dockerfile build-context exclusions for the bootloader image.
#
# Build context = Recto repo ROOT (per docker/bootloader/Dockerfile's
# header comment). This file scopes WHICH files transfer from the
# build-context directory into the Docker daemon. The transfer step
# is naive `tar over a socket`, so the smaller the context, the
# faster the build + the less RAM Docker uses staging the transfer.
#
# Rules: include only what the COPY directives in the Dockerfile
# actually need. Phone-side MAUI source, test suites, dev scripts,
# private/, etc. all get excluded -- they're irrelevant to the
# substrate-side bootloader runtime.

# Phone-side MAUI Blazor project — huge (50+ MB of C# source + assets)
# and irrelevant at runtime.
phone/

# Test suite — only runs in CI, not in production container.
tests/
pytest-cache-files-*/
.pytest_cache/

# Maintainer-side helper scripts. Not substrate runtime concerns.
scripts/
*script_*.ps1
*script.ps1

# Docs — useful for humans, irrelevant at container runtime.
docs/
*.md
!README.md

# Build artifacts + cache directories.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.Python
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# Maintainer-local tree (sometimes present alongside Recto
# repo at the operator's discretion; never part of the image).
private/

# Recto's own development virtualenv if present.
.venv/
venv/

# IDE / editor artifacts.
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo

# CI artifacts.
.github/

# Standalone dev/demo scripts that aren't the canonical launcher.
demo.service.yml
fake_phone.py
recto_ios_redeploy.sh
run_bootloader.py

# Git metadata — not needed inside the image. The image's
# provenance comes from the LABEL directives in the Dockerfile +
# image-tag conventions, not from .git/.
.git/
.gitignore
